From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: preserve Uke raw microphone channel IDs

The native codec-DMA source reports contiguous channel IDs 1,2,3,4. The
quad speaker mapping requests 1,2,4,5 from the frontend MFC, which folds the
third input into the first pair, moves the fourth to output 3 and produces
silence on output 4. Independent decimator attenuation reproduces this on Uke.

Request the matching contiguous IDs only for four-channel capture on graph 2
of the explicit Uke microphone card. Preserve generic mappings, all playback,
other cards and other capture formats. These DSP IDs are transport labels,
not physical microphone locations. No electrical or gain settings change.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
@@ -214,6 +214,7 @@
 static int q6apm_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 			     struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 {
+	struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *soc_prtd = snd_soc_substream_to_rtd(substream);
 	struct snd_pcm_runtime *runtime = substream->runtime;
 	struct q6apm_dai_rtd *prtd = runtime->private_data;
 	struct audioreach_module_config cfg = {};
@@ -236,6 +237,14 @@
 	cfg.bit_width = prtd->bits_per_sample;
 	cfg.fmt = SND_AUDIOCODEC_PCM;
 	audioreach_set_default_channel_mapping(cfg.channel_map, runtime->channels);
+	/* Keep codec-DMA input IDs instead of applying a quad speaker layout. */
+	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE && runtime->channels == 4 &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("xiaomi,uke") && soc_prtd->dai_link->id == 2 &&
+	    of_device_is_compatible(soc_prtd->card->dev->of_node,
+				"xiaomi,uke-microphone-audio-card")) {
+		cfg.channel_map[2] = PCM_CHANNEL_FC;
+		cfg.channel_map[3] = PCM_CHANNEL_LS;
+	}
 	if (prtd->state) {
 		/* clear the previous setup if any  */
 		q6apm_graph_stop(prtd->graph);
